  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing - dependency outage, not storage.\n\n**Current state:**\n- `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` `Up 4 seconds` (E1) and `running: true` (E7).\n- `incidentlab-db-1` is `exited` `Exited (0) 2 seconds ago` (E1), confirmed `running: false`, `status: exited`, `exit_code: 0` (E4).\n- App `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n\n**Why app/uploads fail - symptom:**\n- App logs show `upload` at `/app/main.py line 65` failing in `psycopg.connect` (E3):\n  > `psycopg.OperationalError: failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution`\n- Same error in `health` at `/app/main.py line 113` followed by `health check failed` and `GET /health 503` (E3).\n- This is DNS failure because the `db` host does not exist while `incidentlab-db-1` is stopped. Both containers are on `incidentlab_default` network when running (E4,E7), and app bind-mount is intact `bind /srv/lab-data -> /data rw: true` (E7), user `1000:1000` (E7).\n\n**Root cause - db stopped cleanly, not crashed:**\n- DB logs show normal start `database system is ready to accept connections` then `received fast shutdown request`, `shutting down`, `database system is shut down` (E5). No crash traceback.\n- Inspect shows `oom_killed: false`, `error: null`, `exit_code: 0`, `health: unhealthy`, `restart_count: 0` (E4). App also `oom_killed: false`, `error: null` (E7).\n- `recent_events 60m` shows external `kill`, `stop`, `die exit 0` for `incidentlab-db-1` at `23:57:32`, with no subsequent `start`, while app had `start` at `23:57:29` (E6). Earlier cycles also show `kill/stop/die/destroy/rename/start` with `pg_isready` health checks `healthy` (E6). Pattern is orderly stop, not OOM/crash.\n\n**Ruled out storage causes:**\n- Filesystem for `/srv/lab-data`: `use_percent: 9.0`, `available_mb: 410.6`, `inode_use_percent: 0.2` (E8) - not full.\n- `/srv/lab-data/uploads`: `is_dir: true`, `owner 1000:1000` matches `app 1000:1000`, `mode 0755`, `app_user_can_write: true` (E9) - writable, no permission block. App mount is `rw: true` (E7).\n\nConclusion: Uploads and health fail as a symptom of unavailable dependency `incidentlab-db-1` being stopped. Storage full and permission denied are ruled out by E8 and E9. Repairs require human approval - no changes made.\n",
